---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Eddie" description="About Eddie, a designer and frontend developer outside Stockholm.">
  <div class="about">
    <article class="about__inner">
      <h1 class="visually-hidden">About Ed</h1>

      <div class="about-lead">
        <p class="p-intro">
          Hey, I'm Ed. Designer, frontend developer and compulsive
          pixel-nudger, living just outside Stockholm. I make websites,
          interfaces, and other things that live on screens, and I care an
          unreasonable amount about how they feel.
        </p>
        <figure class="about-photo">
          <img
            src="/images/me.jpeg"
            alt="Eddie standing outside by a lake"
            width="828"
            height="1283"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </figure>
      </div>

      <p class="p-punch">Creative by nature.<br />Technical by effort.</p>

      <p class="p-body p-tilt-left">
        I've been a creative person for as long as I can remember. I went to a
        Waldorf school, where drawing, painting, and making things with your
        hands were the whole point, and it stuck. Computers were always
        around too, and I liked them a lot. I was just never the brainiac type
        who lived in the terminal.
      </p>

      <p class="p-body p-offset-right">
        That mix is exactly why UI and UX design pulled me in. I studied web
        development at university, then frontend engineering at vocational
        school, and I still genuinely enjoy programming. It's just not my
        forte. Design is: the point where code becomes something a person can
        see, use, and hopefully enjoy.
      </p>

      <p class="p-display">Almost right<br />isn't right.</p>

      <p class="p-body">
        What I bring is care. I notice when a margin is two pixels off. I'll
        spend an embarrassingly long time nudging a letter-spacing value.
        Perfection isn't a realistic goal, but the last few percent of
        attention is the difference between something that works and something
        that feels right.
      </p>

      <p class="p-outro">
        It should work.<br />
        It should feel right.<br />
        It should look like <strong>someone cared</strong>.
      </p>

      <p class="p-note">
        <a href="https://nope.digital">nope</a> is the studio I'm building all
        of this under. The <a href="/writing">writing</a> lives here.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    width: 100%;
    flex: 1;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    background: var(--2);
    color: var(--3);
  }

  .about__inner {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--max-width-site);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 7vw, 5rem) var(--space-container)
      clamp(5rem, 12vw, 9rem);
  }

  .about p {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-family-prose);
    color: var(--3);
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .visually-hidden {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .about-lead {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    margin-bottom: clamp(4rem, 9vw, 7rem);
  }

  .about .p-intro {
    max-width: 44ch;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .about-photo {
    flex: 0 0 clamp(14rem, 30vw, 20rem);
    margin: 0;
    transform: rotate(1.5deg);
  }

  /* me.jpeg has white letterbox bars baked into the file; the real photo
     occupies rows 357-960 of 1283. A 3/2 crop at 51.5% stays inside it. */
  .about-photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    aspect-ratio: 3 / 2;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: 50% 51.5%;
  }

  .about .p-punch {
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6rem);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold);
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em;
  }

  .about .p-body {
    max-width: 48ch;
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .about .p-tilt-left {
    max-width: 44ch;
    transform: rotate(-1.5deg);
  }

  .about .p-offset-right {
    max-width: 40ch;
    margin-inline-start: auto;
    transform: rotate(1deg);
  }

  .about .p-display {
    margin-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 8rem);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-black);
    line-height: var(--line-height-display);
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .about .p-outro {
    max-width: 24ch;
    margin-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
    font-family: var(--font-family-base);
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold);
    line-height: 1.3;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .about .p-outro strong {
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-black);
  }

  .about .p-note {
    max-width: 40ch;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .about .p-note a {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: var(--space-1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 700px) {
    .about-lead {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .about-photo {
      flex-basis: auto;
      width: min(78vw, 22rem);
      align-self: flex-end;
    }

    .about .p-offset-right {
      max-width: 44ch;
    }
  }
</style>
